{
 "title": "Basic shaders part 2: clear coat, glass, a candle, cloth",
 "summary": "More materials for the library, each marked as an asset: clear coat (dark purple, roughness 0, Coat weight 1, a noise through a weak bump for wet paint), glass (transmission 1, roughness 0.02) on a subdivided Suzanne; a candle modelled from a cylinder (the top inset and dipped, a wick inset, extruded and bent, random top faces pushed down as melted wax, bevel + subdivision) on a yellow base, a flame from a UV sphere pulled up with proportional editing (emission 40), wax with subsurface and a black rough wick in its own material slot; a cloth simulation (a plane subdivided 50 times with Cloth physics and self collision dropped on a collision icosphere, subdivided and solidified) in red fabric (magic + noise textures mixed into a bump).",
 "objects": [
  {
   "name": "ClearCoatBall",
   "description": "clear coat"
  },
